<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills. [CORRECTED 07:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills. [CORRECTED 07:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose to 10.257 percent (corrects from 10.285 percent) on Thursday from 10.256 percent at the previous auction on August 22.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Nov 28, 1996 (Nov 21, 1996)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.257 percent (corrects) (10.256)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 925.725 million (535.650 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 976.425 million (595.650 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.002-10.285 percent (10.002-10.297)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.002-10.500 percent (10.002-10.500)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 152 (95)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 168 (99)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
